tado-coordinator — third-party components
=========================================

This project's own source code and documentation are licensed under the MIT
License; see LICENSE.

It also uses, without redistributing, third-party components under their own
licenses:

1. freedo — reference/freedo, a git submodule (https://github.com/CappyT/freedo)
   Licensed under the Apache License 2.0. Used as a protocol reference and a
   test oracle: tools/golden runs freedo's builders to generate
   golden/vectors.txt, and the gateway tests replay freedo's captured frames.
   No freedo code is part of the firmware or the gateway.

2. TI CoreSDK for CC13xx/CC26xx — NOT included in this repository.
   The CC1312 firmware builds against driverlib and the startup code of the
   TI CoreSDK, installed separately (see firmware/README.md). It is
   Copyright (c) Texas Instruments Incorporated and licensed under
   BSD-3-Clause; consult the SDK's own license.

3. ESP-IDF and esp-mqtt — NOT included in this repository.
   The gateway firmware builds against Espressif's ESP-IDF and the esp-mqtt
   component, fetched by the ESP-IDF build. Licensed under the Apache
   License 2.0.

